## STEP 5 — SCREEN 3: Shots

This is the main working screen. It has a shot list with scene context columns, inline editing, and a tasks sub-panel that appears below when a shot row is clicked.

### 5a — Add nav item
Left sidebar → **+ Add page** → Name: `Shots` → Icon: camera

### 5b — Queries

---

**Query: `get_shots`**
- Run: On page load
- SQL:
```sql
SELECT
  sh.id,
  sh.shot_code,
  sh.status,
  sh.complexity,
  sh.priority,
  sh.description,
  sh.vfx_description,
  sh.vfx_notes,
  sh.internal_notes,
  sh.tags,
  sh.plate_duration_frames,
  sh.frame_rate,
  sh.resolution,
  sh.cut_duration_frames,
  sh.first_frame,
  sh.last_frame,

  -- Scene context
  sc.scene_number,
  sc.slug_line,
  sc.int_ext,
  sc.time_of_day,
  sc.start_page,
  sc.end_page,
  sc.page_count,
  sc.location_name,
  sc.has_vfx        AS scene_has_vfx,

  -- Task summary
  COUNT(t.id)       AS task_count,
  COALESCE(SUM(t.estimated_cost), 0) AS estimated_cost

FROM shots sh
LEFT JOIN scenes sc ON sc.id = sh.scene_id
LEFT JOIN tasks t   ON t.shot_id = sh.id
WHERE sh.project_id = {{ selected_project.id }}
  AND sh.deleted_at IS NULL
  AND (
    {{ sel_episode_filter.value }} = '' OR
    sh.episode_id = {{ sel_episode_filter.value }}::uuid
  )
  AND (
    {{ sel_status_filter.value }} = '' OR
    sh.status = {{ sel_status_filter.value }}
  )
GROUP BY sh.id, sc.id
ORDER BY sc.scene_number, sh.shot_code;
```

