## STEP 9 — Polish Tips

**Color-code complexity** on the shots table using a custom column renderer:
```
{{ ['','🟢','🔵','🟡','🟠','🔴'][currentRow.complexity] || '—' }} {{ currentRow.complexity }}
```

**Page count display** — Retool doesn't natively format eighths, so use a custom column:
```js
{{
  const v = currentRow.page_count;
  if (!v) return '—';
  const whole = Math.floor(v);
  const frac = Math.round((v - whole) * 8);
  const fracs = ['','⅛','¼','⅜','½','⅝','¾','⅞'];
  return whole + (frac ? fracs[frac] : '') + ' pp';
}}
```

**Freeze the first two columns** (Shot, Scene) in `tbl_shots` so they stay visible when scrolling right — set `Frozen` to true on those columns in the table settings.

**Keyboard shortcut tip:** In Retool tables, pressing Enter on a selected row opens inline editing. Escape discards. Tab moves between cells.

